vscode: typing, Ctrl+S, Ctrl+Z
open: standup.md

@brief
Vim starts in NORMAL mode. Normal mode is not "broken" - it is the
mode where every letter on your keyboard is a command. You only type
text after you have deliberately asked to.

Three things to do in standup.md:

  1. Fix the typo "Yesterdya" -> "Yesterday"
  2. Delete the whole "TODO:" line
  3. In its place, add a line:  - Blocked: nothing

Then save and quit.

Make a mess on purpose at some point and undo it with  u  .
Redo with  Ctrl-R  . You cannot break anything here.

@keys
i        INSERT mode, typing starts before the cursor
a        INSERT mode, typing starts after the cursor
Esc      back to NORMAL mode. When lost, press Esc.
x        delete the character under the cursor
dd       delete the whole line
o        open a new line below and start typing
u        undo        Ctrl-R  redo
:w       write (save)        :q  quit        :wq  both
:q!      quit and throw away changes

@hints
The typo is a swap: "dya" should be "day". Put the cursor on the
wrong character and press x to delete it, then a to append the
letter back in the right place. Esc when done.
--
To kill a line, put the cursor anywhere on it and press dd. The
whole line disappears, no selecting required.
--
Press o on the line above where you want the new text. It opens a
blank line below and drops you into INSERT mode in one keystroke.
Then type the line, press Esc, then :wq and Enter.

@solution
/Yesterdya   Enter        jump to the typo
fy                        hop to the y in "dya"
x                         delete it  -> "Yesterda"
a y  Esc                  append "y" -> "Yesterday"   (or just: cw Yesterday Esc)

G                         last line (the TODO line)
cc                        clear the line, stay in INSERT
- Blocked: nothing        type it
Esc
:wq Enter

The mental model: you are not "in a text box". You are issuing
commands, and INSERT mode is one of the commands.

@start standup.md
# Standup - Tuesday

- Yesterdya: finished the order repository
- Today: start on the resolver
- TODO: delete this line before posting

@expected standup.md
# Standup - Tuesday

- Yesterday: finished the order repository
- Today: start on the resolver
- Blocked: nothing
